body: "Non-blocking finding from the pre-merge review of #110 (src/read_session.rs:430): lossy filename conversion gives identical snapshot hashes for distinct Unix filenames such as `tasks/\\x80.toon` and `tasks/\\x81.toon` with identical contents. Either reject non-UTF-8 filenames with a typed refusal or hash the exact filename bytes, so the certificate's filename guarantee holds. Acceptance: a Unix-only regression with two such files produces distinct hashes (or a typed refusal) and fails on revert.\n\n---\n\n### GitHub comments (1)\n\n> **@unbraind** (2026-10-23T22:54:54Z)\n>\n> Fixed in #110 (exact filename bytes are hashed; regressions fail on revert)."
